1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manuchar_II_Dadiani
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuchar II Dadiani (Georgian: მანუჩარ II დადიანი; died c. 1840[1]), of the House of Dadiani, was Prince of Mingrelia from 1791 to 1793 as a rival to his elder brother, Grigol Dadiani, whose rule was marred by the long-standing st
2 CONC ruggle between the Imeretian crown seeking to subdue Mingrelia and Mingrelian efforts to win full independence, a continuation of the conflict which had plagued western Georgia for centuries. After the brothers reconciled in 1799,
2 CONC  Manuchar was appanaged with Salipartiano, which he lost to his nephew Levan, a new Prince of Mingrelia, in the wake of Grigol's death in 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuchar was a son of Katsia II Dadiani by his third wife Anna Tsulukidze.
2 CONT
2 CONT Manuchar was married to Darejan, daughter of the Abkhaz nobleman Zurab Shervashidze. He had seven children, whose descendants are still extant:
2 CONT
2 CONT Katsia (born 1795),
2 CONT Zurab,
2 CONT Levan (born 1807),
2 CONT Ekaterine (born 1814),
2 CONT Giorgi (died c. 1864),
2 CONT Aleksandre (died 1856),
2 CONT Dutu (born 1820).
2 CONT ___
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.royalark.net/Georgia/mingrel5.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 1791 - 1793 His Splendour The Pious Prince of High Rank Manuchari [Mamuka], Duke of Dukes of Mingrelia, fourth son of His Splendour The Pious Prince of High Rank Katsia II Dadiani, Duke of Dukes of Mingrelia. Prince of Salipartian
2 CONC o before his accession. Rebelled and deposed his elder brother, 1791. Deposed by his younger brother, Tariel 1793. m. (first) a daughter of Prince Shervashidze. m. (second) Her Splendour The Pious Princess of High Rank Ana Dadiani
2 CONC , daughter of Prince Kakhaberidze-Chijavadze. He d. after 1804, having had issue, six sons and three daughters (ancestor of the Modidanakhsky branch):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Prince Katsia Manuchari Dadiani. b. 1795.
2 CONT 2) Prince Zurabi Manuchari Dadiani
2 CONT 3) Prince Dutu Manuchari Dadiani. b. 1789.
2 CONT 4) Prince Levanti Manuchari Dadiani. b. 1815
2 CONT 5) Prince Aleksandri Manuchari Dadiani
2 CONT 6) Prince Giorgi Manuchari Dadiani
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Princess Elisabed Mze-Khatun. b. 1798
2 CONT 2) Princess Kethevan Dadiani. b. 1814.
2 CONT 3) Princess Matha Dadiani.
