1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Prince '''Nikita Sergeievitch Trubetzkoy'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 07/01/1877, Tiflis - 08/31/1963, Petit-Clamaret, Paris, France Orthodox. Father - actual privy councilor Sergei Nikitich, mother - Sophia Iraklievna ur. Princess Bagration-Mukhranskaya.
2 CONT
2 CONT Education: Corps of Pages (1898, 1st category, in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod Regiment). Ranks: entered the service (1.09.1896), cornet with st. 08.13.1897 (High pr. 1898), lieutenant (Art. 08.13.1901), staff captain (Art. 08
2 CONC .13.1905), captain (Art. 08.13.1909), transferred to the Guard (1913 or 1914), colonel ... Service: he studied in the Corps of Pages (1893-1898, entered the 5th grade), in the 44th Dragoon Nizhny Novgorod regiment, adjutant led. P
2 CONC rince Nikolai Mikhailovich (before 09/01/1912 - after 09/01/1913). Awards: A3 (High pr. 1909), C2 (High pr. 1912).
2 CONT
2 CONT Other information: in exile in France, in 1934 treasurer, secretary and member of the court of honor of the main board of the Union of Pages, by Feb. 1954 Chairman of the Union of Pages, 1934 General Secretary of the Society of Fr
2 CONC iends of the "Sentinel", 1939 supported the leader. Prince Vladimir Kirillovich; board member of the Union of Officers of the Caucasian Army in Paris, secretary of the regimental association of the 17th dragoon regiment, chairman 
2 CONC of the Society of Zealots of Russian Military Antiquity.
2 CONT
2 CONT Works:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nizhny Novgorod saber // Mollo "Russian edged weapons". Paris, 196? Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Volkov S.V. Army Cavalry Officers: The Martyrology Experience. - M .: Russian way, 2004. List of captains of army cavalry by seniority, 1.09.1912.
2 CONT
2 CONT List of captains of army cavalry by seniority, 09/01/1913.
2 CONT
2 CONT von Freiman O.R. Pages for 185 Years, no. 9, Friedrichshamn, 1897. 
2 CONT
