1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.royalark.net/Georgia/mingrel5.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT i) Prince Beglari Giorgi Davit Dadiani. b. 1857. m. Princess Natalia Grigorievna Dadiani (b. 30th July 1865 o.s.; d. at Chisinau, Bessarabia, 18th October 1903 o.s., bur. there at the Central Orthodox (Armenian) Cemetery), Founder
2 CONC  & Dir of the The Chisinau Girls’ Gymnasium (Princess Dadiani Gymnasium), and Founder of the Soc for the Promotion of Secondary Education, Grigori Godlewski, of Tighina, a Russian nobleman of Polish heritage, settled in Bessarabia
2 CONC . He d. 1947, having had issue, one son and two daughters:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Prince Boris Beglari Dadiani. b. 14th June 1896 o.s. He d.v.p. s.p. (believed drowned) 13th June 1913 (bur. beside his mother at the Central Orthodox (Armenian) Cemetery, Chisinau, Bessarabia).
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Princess Thamar Dadiani. b. 1897. m. Prince Filimoni [Chutu] Datu Chikovani (b. 1888; d. 1924). She d. 1930.
2 CONT (2) Princess Lili Dadiani. b. 1902. She d. 1974, having had issue, two sons, who assumed the name of Dadiani.
2 CONT (3) Princess Nina. m. Prince Chikovani.
