3 CTRY Russian Federation
1 DEAT
2 DATE 31 DEC 1929
2 ADDR
3 CITY Havana
3 STAE Havana
3 CTRY Cuba
1 OCCU Pilot
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Luitenant pilot and Tzarist diplomat to France under Nicholas II, the last Tzar of Russia. Member of the Order of St. Vladimir. Died in Havana Cuba in 1929 from a burst appendix while building the Carretera Central
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Moscow to a Russian princess. He met his wife in Paris in 1917 where he studied civil engineering and architecture at the Sorbonne had a post at the Tzarist embassy. They married in October of 1917, twice on the same day; 
2 CONC first in the Russian Orthodox Church on Rue Daru at 11am, and then at noon in the Catholic Church of Saint Ferdinand in the La Estrella neighborhood.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his wife Hilda fled in 1918 France after the October Revolution because France had allied itself with the new government and was incarcerating Russians in internment camps. Alexander and Hilda moved to Cuba, where they set 
2 CONC up a house in el Vedado. He had studied civil engineering in Paris and had a role in working on the Carretera Central in Cuba, which began to be built in 1927.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died of peritonitis in 1929. His appendix burst while in Oriente and he was flown to the Havana Martínez Fortún Clinic where he passed away. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: We knew the name of his first wife and her parents from Nora Antonia de Cardenas. Using that information we discovered the following:
2 CONT
