1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===1305th Knight of the Order of the Golden Fleece: Austrian Branch===
2 CONT * [http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Adam_II._%28Liechtenstein%29 '''Hans Adam II von Liechtenstein'''] - Wikipedia - German
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans-Adam_II,_Prince_of_Liechtenstein '''Hans Adam II, Prince of Liechtenstein'''] - Wikipedia - English
2 CONT * [http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans-Adam_II_de_Liechtenstein '''Hans-Adam de Liechtenstein'''] - Wikipedia - French
2 CONT * [http://www.allthingsroyal.nl/koninklijkefamilies/liechtenstein/troonsopvolging.php '''next in line for the Liechtenstein crown'''] - in Dutch
2 CONT * '''born''' - 14 Feb 1945, Zurich Switserland
2 CONT * '''father''' - Franz Joseph II
2 CONT * '''mother''' - Georgina von Wilczek
2 CONT * '''married to''' - Marie Aglae Kinsky von Wchnitz und Tettau (b.14 April 1940) on 30 July 1967
2 CONT * '''children''' - 
2 CONT # Alois von Liechtenstein
2 CONT #  Maximilian von Liechtenstein
2 CONT # Constantin von Liechtenstein
2 CONT # Tatjana von Liechtenstein
2 CONT ==Powers==
2 CONT The Prince of Liechtenstein has broad powers; a referendum to adopt Hans-Adam's revision of the constitution to expand his powers passed in 2003.  The changes also included a republican option, whereby the Prince was henceforth fo
2 CONC rmally barred from vetoing any bill to establish a republic.  In addition, the right of each of the parishes which make up the Principality to secede was recognised.  Prince Hans-Adam had announced his intention for him and his fa
2 CONC mily to move to Austria if the referendum failed.  Despite opposition from Mario Frick, a former prime minister, the Prince's referendum motion was carried by the electorate.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 15 Aug. 2004 Prince Hans-Adam II formally turned the power of making day-to-day governmental decisions over to his eldest son, Prince Alois, as a way of beginning a dynastic transition to a new generation. Legally, Hans- Adam r
2 CONC emains Head of State.
2 CONT ==Personal life==
2 CONT On 30 July 1967, at Vaduz, Liechtenstein, he married his second cousin once-removed, Countess Maarie Aglaë Kinsky von Wchinitz und Tattau (born 1940) who, upon her husband's accession to the throne, became ''Her Serene Highness th
2 CONC e Princess of Liechtenstein''.  Their official residence is at Vaduz Castle, which overlooks the capital. (car)
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Adam II. (voller Name: Johannes Adam Ferdinand Alois Josef Maria Marko d'Aviano Pius von und zu Liechtenstein; * 14. Februar 1945  in Zürich, Schweiz) ist regierender Fürst und Staatsoberhaupt Liechtensteins.
2 CONT
